\p \v 14 \wj \w For|strong="G1063"\w* \w it is just like|strong="G5618"\w* \w a man|strong="G444"\w* \w going on a journey|strong="G589"\w*, \w who called|strong="G2564"\w* \w his|strong="G2398"\w* \w servants|strong="G1401"\w* \w and|strong="G2532"\w* \w entrusted|strong="G3860"\w* \w them|strong="G846"\w* \w with his|strong="G846"\w* \w possessions|strong="G5225"\w*.\wj* \v 15 \wj \w To one|strong="G3739"\w* \w he gave|strong="G1325"\w* \w five|strong="G4002"\w* \w talents|strong="G5007"\w*,\f + \fr 25:15 \ft A talent was worth about twenty years’ wages for a laborer.\f* \w to another|strong="G3739"\w* \w two talents|strong="G1417"\w*, \w and|strong="G1161"\w* \w to another|strong="G3739"\w* \w one talent|strong="G1520"\w* — \w each|strong="G1538"\w* \w according to|strong="G2596"\w* \w his own|strong="G2398"\w* \w ability|strong="G1411"\w*. \w And|strong="G2532"\w* \w he went on his journey|strong="G589"\w*.\wj*
